# ProEQ — what stays out of git (and why)
# Policy "Tier A": KiCad sources + BOM + small CAD deliverables are tracked.
# Fabrication outputs and heavy 3D data ship as GitHub Release assets instead.

# --- OS / editor debris --------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# KiCad local UI state: window geometry, visible layers, zoom, last plot dir.
# Decision: ignored. Pure per-machine noise, changes on every pan and zoom.
*.kicad_prl

# --- KiCad transients, autosaves and backup trees ------------------------
_autosave-*
*-backups/
ProjectEQ-backups/
fp-info-cache
.history*

# --- fabrication outputs (Release assets) --------------------------------
# Gerber/drill plots, JLC/PCBWay packages, CPL + position files, IPC netlist.
Gerber/
Gerber V1 old/
jlcpcb/
production/
PLOTS/
plots/
*.zip
# full duplicate of the main board inside the laser-cut folder (19 MB)
SVG for cut/ProjectEQ.kicad_pcb

# --- heavy CAD (Release assets) ------------------------------------------
ProjectEQ.step
ProjectEQ_V2.pcb3d
Board_render.blend
*.blend
*.blend1
*.FCBak
*.stl
VLP model + ring/step/
VLP model + ring/VLP Vu/*.step

# --- stale duplicates of the same design ---------------------------------
ProjectEQ-backup.*
ProjectEQ_backup.kicad_pcb
ProjectEQ_backup.kicad_pro
*rearrangeled*
*.bak

# --- private notes, not project material ---------------------------------
# Personal diary, no technical content. Kept on disk, deliberately not published.
board installation timeline
